{"name":"Cardoon","hex":"#9aae8c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cardoon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any member of the species Cynara cardunculus of prickly perennial plants which has leaf stalks eaten as a vegetable, related to the artichoke."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cardoon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cardoon","blocks":[{"text":"The cardoon, also called the artichoke thistle, is a thistle in the family Asteraceae. It is a naturally occurring species that also has many cultivated forms, including the globe artichoke. It is native to the Mediterranean region, where it was domesticated in ancient times and still occurs as a wild plant."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Cynara_cardunculus_flavescens_%2814684164583%29.jpg/330px-Cynara_cardunculus_flavescens_%2814684164583%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cardoon","wikidata":"Q7186137"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Cynara_cardunculus_-_Royal_Botanical_Garden%2C_Madrid.JPG/500px-Cynara_cardunculus_-_Royal_Botanical_Garden%2C_Madrid.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Cynara_cardunculus_-_Royal_Botanical_Garden%2C_Madrid.JPG/1280px-Cynara_cardunculus_-_Royal_Botanical_Garden%2C_Madrid.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Cynara_cardunculus_-_Royal_Botanical_Garden%2C_Madrid.JPG/500px-Cynara_cardunculus_-_Royal_Botanical_Garden%2C_Madrid.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cultivated cardoon foliage, Madrid Royal Botanical Garden, without leaf spines.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACynara_cardunculus_-_Royal_Botanical_Garden%2C_Madrid.J